{
 "note": "Measured, not chosen: godot/tests/test_biomes.gd computes the luminance contrast (WCAG ratio) of every lake object, Atlas trace and D6 own drawing against the five biome backgrounds (DiveCore.biome_contrast, TABOO 0.3 rule 59) and lists here what falls below 1.5.  The test fails on any new entry and on any entry that no longer fails, so this list is the honest state.  See docs/HLD_DIVE_BIOMES_BUBBLES_2026-09-30.md, phase P3.",
 "reasons": {
  "lake": "Real colours of real things (scripts/lake/lake_objects.py, TABOO 0.07): mid-tone stone, iron, clay and wood sit at the luminance of lit water in the shallows, and brown things on brown silt are true camouflage.  The data does not allow repainting them; readability must come from the lamp, shading and silhouette (open question in the HLD).",
  "atlas": "Trace colours come from the chorus data (scripts/story/atlas_nodes.py) and atlas_traces.gd, owned elsewhere; leather, dark iron and grey stone are true to the things.  Reported to the owner, not repainted here.",
  "d6": "Own drawings in natural palette (neutral_procedural.py): mid-grey boulders and quartz, olive reed and pondweed, dark beams.  Mean colour of the opaque pixels; the drawings keep their inner shading, which this mean does not see."
 },
